	abstract = {To comprehensively address the challenges of insertion loss (IL), reflection, and noise in high-speed PAM4 signal transmission, this paper proposes a digital equalization scheme for SerDes receivers based on an ADC+DSP architecture. To mitigate IL and reflection effects, the main equalizer employs a hybrid structure combining a 16-tap fixed-tap feed-forward equalizer (FFE) with a 4-tap floating-tap FFE (FT-FFE). An optimized grouping configuration for the FT-FFE achieves a 75% reduction in latency. To enhance noise immunity, a two-tap speculative pre-decision and loop-refactored decision feedback equalizer (SP-LR DFE) utilizing pre-classification and loop reconstruction is implemented, reducing complexity while increasing timing margin. The proposed digital equalization scheme is experimentally validated on an FPGA platform, achieving a bit error rate (BER) below 10<sup>−12</sup> over a channel with 39 dB insertion loss. The scheme expands the bathtub curve eye width by 0.2 UI, requiring only marginal increases in area (7%) and power consumption (2.5%) versus prior work. © 2025},
